  "hypothesis": "Required terrain map-character readers reject full JS strings whose valid C prefix ends at an embedded NUL.",
  "expectedBehavior": "T followed by NUL accepts and paints TREE for table and positional forms; plain T accepts, TT and leading-NUL controls reject.",
  "observedBehavior": "C accepts four target calls and paintsTREE13; JS errors and retainsROOM25. Six controls match.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "production_api",
    "scope": "Public JS des.terrain table/positional calls versus exact C wrappers/readers/writers, preserving NUL-bearing bytes in fixed typed adapters; four targets and six controls.",
    "limitations": [
      "Two supported des.terrain forms: explicit table and positional x,y,typ. Fixed default frame1,0, relative13,10, initial ROOM from solidfill. Only TREE painting and input acceptance are compared; no tree/monster/object/player runtime effects or finalization.",
      "C executes exact lspo_level_init/lspo_terrain, terrain writers, get_table_mapchr/get_table_str, dupstr, check_mapchr and splev_chr2typ plus the exact char2typ table. Fixed typed Lua-reader adapters preserve raw string bytes and only emulate these explicit argument forms, integer coordinates and table fields. No Lua library dependency or general coercion/VM claim.",
      "Hex transport preserves embedded NUL and suffix in the input allocation. Actual C dupstr/strlen determines prefix behavior; the adapter does not pre-truncate. The table path copies the C prefix; the positional path passes the original bytes to exact check_mapchr.",
      "Coordinate adapter asserts in-bounds explicit values and default frame1,0 with no room/random selection. Unused parser/selection and runtime-effect adapters abort. nhl_error adapter longjmps to capture failure; error text/stack/process behavior is not asserted.",
      "Four targets cover T-NUL-suffix and T-NUL in both forms. Six controls cover plain T acceptance, TT rejection and leading-NUL rejection. Rejected controls validate parsing boundaries only; they are not invalid-setup negatives.",
      "This extends the existing C-string-prefix cause (message, engraving, map) to a required map-character reader. No new independent repair identity, broad string equivalence, shipped exposure or score-impact claim."
    ]
  },
